Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, xwayland
Suggests: foot
Description: wlroots compositor with an infinite scroll workspace
 dwlm is a fork of dwl, a tiling Wayland compositor based on wlroots and
 SceneFX (fx renderer with rounded corners).
 .
 It adds a Niri-like horizontal scroll layout: windows stack in columns on
 an infinite strip that is panned with the mouse wheel or a two-finger
 touchpad swipe, with an animated viewport, per-column workspaces,
 rule-based floating windows, and whole-column moves between monitors,
 alongside the classic dwm tiling layouts.